    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine how many books are left over after repacking them into boxes of 40 each, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of books:**\n   Each box contains 39 books, and there are 1335 boxes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of books} = 1335 \\times 39\n   \\]\n\n2. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 40 = 53400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 1 = 1335\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 39 = 53400 - 1335 = 52065\n   \\]\n   So, the total number of books is 52065.\n\n3. **Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of full boxes} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{52065}{40} \\right\\rfloor\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{52065}{40} = 1301.625\n   \\]\n   The integer part of 1301.625 is 1301. Therefore, the number of full boxes is 1301.\n\n4. **Calculate the number of books in these full boxes:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books in full boxes} = 1301 \\times 40 = 52040\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the number of books left over:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Books left over} = 52065 - 52040 = 25\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of books left over after repacking as many boxes of 40 books each as possible is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).",
